And the caller keeps them apart:
.github/workflows/account-skill-zips.yml:252-253
  print(message, file=sys.stderr)
  print(status)

Only `print(status)` reaches `verdict=$( ... )`. `$(...)` also strips trailing newlines, so even a `\n` cannot survive; a `\r` could, but only if a literal carried one.

