Once `_guard` is refactored into a shared `_shell_block(body, opener_regex)`, the FROM_RUN guard is a five-line addition, not a new subsystem. Add to TestSkillInputIsValidatedBeforeUse (or a sibling class):

    def _run_guard(self):
        return _shell_block(<record step body>, re.compile(r'(?<![\w.-])case\s+"\$FROM_RUN"'))

    @pytest.mark.parametrize("good", ["32414713598", "1"])
    def test_it_admits_a_numeric_run_id(self, good): ...
    @pytest.mark.parametrize("evil", ["", "12a", "1 2", "-1", "1;id", "1\nfoo=bar"])
    def test_it_refuses_anything_that_is_not_a_run_id(self, evil): ...

Delivered through env, like `_bash` already does, and with the same byte-count delivery check — the newline case is the one that matters and it is the one argv would eat.
